  "notes": "Official cause code is TBD/provisional on FORM-366; narrative attributes the event to a weld leak in the Exciter End stator coil cooling water manifold of the Unit 2 Main Generator, causing increased hydrogen usage and a low hydrogen pressure annunciator, prompting a manual reactor trip per procedure. AFW actuated automatically as expected and is modeled as a mitigating/backup system since it responded during the event, not merely design context. No inoperable SSCs contributed to the event. No similar events in the prior three years, so no SIMILAR_TO stub LER emitted. Hydrogen gas system described as part of turbine generator system per narrative background; no EIIS code given for either system, so eiis_code left null per rule 2."
